# routes::graphs::list_source_groups/get_source_group). Required by the
# RLS-scoping discipline every read in routes/graphs.rs already follows
# (graph_account_id -> begin_member_scoped -> `_scoped` Store methods) — not a
# new pattern, and the whole point of the pair is to REPLACE list_sources's
# O(atoms) Rust walk (expand + atom_titles_and_excerpts + atom_inline_content
# PER ATOM — 15.2s in prod on a ~20k-atom ocean), not add to it:
#   source_groups_scoped               — channel-level aggregate rollup (one
#         grouped SQL statement over atoms/node_atoms) backing the list
#         route; O(atoms) inside Postgres, O(groups) in application code.
