# Raised 146 -> 147 PgPool files (2026-09-05): backend/src/bin/
# migrate_personal_to_member_ocean.rs, the one-shot personal-ocean -> org
# member-ocean content migrator that implements the content move
# scripts/migrate_shared_db_org.sh has specified-but-refused since it was
# written. It CANNOT route through the `Store` trait, and that is the point
# rather than an omission: `Store` is bound to a single scope in a single
# database, and this tool exists precisely to span TWO — reading the
# consumer/control plane and writing an org's Neon tenant, decrypting under
# one account DEK and re-encrypting under another. An opaque `Db<'a>` from
# `store.begin(scope)` cannot express a two-database operation.
# Identical in shape and justification to every other one-shot already
# frozen here — bin/export_member_ocean.rs, bin/reextract.rs,
# bin/migrate_control.rs, bin/migrate_tenants.rs and the backfill_* family:
# an operator-run binary that owns its own pools and never serves a request.
# It is also deliberately OUT of scripts/check_no_cross_plane_promotion.sh's
# SCAN_DIRS (routes/services/mcp) for the same reason — backend/src/bin is
# the sanctioned home for cross-plane work, per that guard and per
# migrate_shared_db_org.sh's own header. Not a new pattern this raise
# introduces, and not a conversion site the restructure gains: the file has
# no request-path callers.
