# get_node_candidates` called it AFTER their scoped read transaction
# already committed, ambient on `self.pool`: under the real, non-BYPASSRLS
# `coralswarm_app` role this either hard-errors or silently sees nothing,
# and `unwrap_or_default()` was swallowing that into empty titles for the
# whole page — the opposite of what this PR's own founder requirement
# promises. This is exactly the ratchet's photo-finish case (a GENUINE new
# twin, not a workaround), not a new pattern: it completes an existing
# quartet of siblings rather than introducing a new one, and closing it any
# other way (moving the read into the caller's existing `Db`/scope handle)
# is the restructure this ratchet is deferring, not a same-day fix.
