# Raised by one PgPool file (COR-82, 2026-10-14): `tenancy/read_only_poison.rs`
# heals a pooled server connection left in `default_transaction_read_only =
# on`. It holds a transaction per probe so PgBouncer links a distinct server
# to each, reads that backend's GUC, and runs `pg_terminate_backend` on it.
# That is pool plumbing, not data access: no `Store` method or `Db<'a>` scope
# can name "the server connection behind this acquire", so the restructure
