# Proposed reviewed Library read-model pool-shape registrations.
# Six sites are new on PR4; main registers the pre-existing worker above.
# reason: OPERATOR SQL PROOF. Explicit inventory/reader/control connection pools are required to compare the selected database under its actual physical reader role. Complete inventory rejects row-security-active graphs; actor admission uses the shared scoped control fence and comparisons use Tenant::begin_member_repeatable_read. This registers the operator connection shape as conversion debt, not an exception to caller admission or RLS.
# reason: TEST-SUPPORT ONLY PgPool signatures. shadow_comparison_for_test and runtime_test_support::start are both feature=test-support entrypoints delegating to the real proof runtime. They introduce no bare-pool content query or production Store method; the file-set scanner deliberately does not interpret cfg gates.
# reason: PRODUCTION Library proof orchestration. Retains a control pool for account-scoped proof-ledger operations and fresh shared control admission. Content pairing reauthorizes the Tenant then opens its read-only member-scoped repeatable-read transaction; the control handle is not used as an ambient content executor. Register the retained pool shape as explicit conversion debt.
# reason: OPERATOR ADMISSION. The supplied control pool is used by the shared fresh actor-admission fence and an account-scoped current-role read. Snapshot validation receives an already-scoped transaction. No new Store method or ambient content query is introduced; the pool-bearing operator boundary remains conversion debt.
# reason: PRODUCTION CONTROL LEDGER. ProofWriter privately retains the control pool; every ledger operation opens control_tx, which applies begin_account_scoped for the operator account with bounded statement/lock timeouts. Content comparison receives no exposed writer pool. This registers a concrete conversion site, not blanket permission for unscoped SQL.
# reason: PRODUCTION SHARED ADMISSION FENCE. The new pool-only form first reauthorizes each graph through Tenant, then opens begin_account_scoped on the explicit control pool for current account membership/org binding/revocation. The pool parameter serves bounded background proof admission without retaining AppState; no content table is queried through that bare control pool.
